meta {
  name: Give the Monday its bells
  type: http
  seq: 37
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/calendar-days/{{calendarDayId}}/schedules
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "period_scheme_id": "{{schemeId}}",
    "bell_schedule_id": "{{bellScheduleId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.calendar_day_id: eq {{calendarDayId}}
  res.body.bell_schedule_id: eq {{bellScheduleId}}
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("dayScheduleId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  WITHOUT THIS ROW THE DAY HAS NO CLASSES. Being in session is not enough:
  occurrences are resolved by walking each calendar day's schedules and
  finding the timetable in force for that scheme on that date, so a day with
  no schedule yields an empty list no matter how many slots exist. It is the
  most confusing failure in this feature, because /timetable-calendar happily
  reports the day as open while /timetable-occurrences returns nothing and the
  register refuses with attendance_not_scheduled.

  A day may carry more than one, which is how a school runs two period schemes
  side by side - junior and senior bells on the same date.
}
